{"id": "sdqa0076", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 4.18, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2335, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Cullinan Diamond", "query": "What is the biggest diamond?", "transcript": "What is the biggest diamond?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The biggest diamond ever found is the Cullinan Diamond, discovered in South Africa in 1905. It weighed over 3,000 carats in its rough form and was later cut into several large stones, including one that's part of the British Crown Jewels. If you're asking about the largest polished diamond, that title goes to the Golden Jubilee Diamond, which weighs about 545 carats.", "expert_answer": "The biggest diamond ever found is the **Cullinan Diamond**, discovered in South Africa in 1905.\n\n- **Rough weight:** 3,106 carats  \n- It was later cut into several stones, including the **Great Star of Africa**, which is part of the British Crown Jewels.\n\nIf you mean the biggest **cut/polished** diamond, that is the **Golden Jubilee Diamond**, weighing **545.67 carats**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.7, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 2056}
