{"id": "sdqa0112", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 5.14, "n_chunks": 6, "n_concurrent": 6, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4112, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "1853", "query": "When was the Epic of Gilgamesh discovered?", "transcript": "When was the Epic of Gilgamesh discovered?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The epic of Gilgamesh was rediscovered in the 19th century, when clay tablets containing the text were excavated in the 1850s at the ruins of Nineveh in the library of the Assyrian king Ashurbanipal. Its significance became widely recognized after George Smith identified and translated parts of it in 1872.", "expert_answer": "The **Epic of Gilgamesh** was rediscovered in the **19th century**, when clay tablets containing the text were excavated in the **1850s** at the ruins of **Nineveh** in the library of the Assyrian king **Ashurbanipal**. Its significance became widely recognized after **George Smith** identified and translated parts of it in **1872**.", "expert_latency_s": 2.92, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1699}
