{"id": "sdqa0121", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 4.78, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0891, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "n. When n is a positive integer, exponentiation corresponds to repeated multiplication of the base: that is, bn is the product of multiplying n bas", "query": "What is exponentiation?", "transcript": "What is exponentiation?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Exponentiation is a mathematical operation that means multiplying a number by itself a certain number of times. It's written as a raised to the power of b, where a is the base and b is the exponent or power. For example, 2 raised to the power of 3 equals 2 multiplied by itself three times, which is 8.", "expert_answer": "Exponentiation is a mathematical operation that means multiplying a number by itself a certain number of times.\n\nIt is written as:\n\n\\[\na^b\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n\n- \\(a\\) is the **base**\n- \\(b\\) is the **exponent** or **power**\n\nExample:\n\n\\[\n2^3 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(2^3\\) means “2 raised to the power of 3.”", "expert_latency_s": 2.05, "stall_ms": 23, "relay_ms": 1602}
