{"id": "sdqa0148", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "always", "audio_s": 3.13, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2226, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Thomas Edison", "query": "Who invented the first audio recording device?", "transcript": "Who invented the first audio recording device?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The first audio recording device, the phonautograph, was invented by Édouard-Léon Scott de Martinville in 1857. Thomas Edison later created the phonograph in 1877, which could both record and play back sound.", "expert_answer": "The first audio recording device, the **phonautograph**, was invented by **Édouard-Léon Scott de Martinville** in **1857**.\n\nNote: **Thomas Edison** later invented the **phonograph** in 1877, the first device that could both record **and play back** sound.", "expert_latency_s": 3.3, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1247}
